THE PROJECT &nbsp; 📝 &nbsp;

Form3 is looking for&nbsp;several&nbsp;Senior Software Engineer contractors&nbsp;to&nbsp;work alongside&nbsp;our US Software Engineering team&nbsp;to deliver new&nbsp;products&nbsp;within our US Payments proposition. &nbsp;

This is an opportunity to work on critical payments infrastructure in a highly technical environment, contributing to the design, build, testing and launch of new Zelle and Fedwire capabilities. You’ll be working in Go on Form3’s cloud-native platform, applying proven engineering patterns from our existing payments services while solving the specific challenges that come with high-volume, resilient, regulated payment systems. &nbsp;

• Design and implement new US payments gateway functionality in Go, aligned to product requirements and agreed technical architecture.&nbsp;This includes&nbsp;payment flows, scheme-specific behaviours, error handling, validation and operational requirements, as well as&nbsp;comprehensive automated integration tests covering this functionality. &nbsp;

• Work collaboratively&nbsp;with Product, Engineering&nbsp;and other&nbsp;functions&nbsp;to refine requirements and validate implementation choices. &nbsp;

• Contribute to technical design activity, including design proposals, implementation plans and problem-solving within&nbsp;Form3&nbsp;platform&nbsp;architecture. &nbsp;

• Support non-functional requirements related&nbsp;to resilience, performance, disaster recovery, failure-mode testing and operational readiness.&nbsp;Establish and improve monitoring, alerting, telemetry and observability to support operational visibility from development through to production. &nbsp;

• Support production-readiness activity, including release preparation, final validation, production deployment and post-launch issue resolution. &nbsp;

• Produce and maintain technical documentation, including design notes, testing documentation, deployment guidance, operational procedures and runbooks. &nbsp;

• Ensure all work aligns with Form3’s engineering standards, security expectations and the standards required for critical payments infrastructure. &nbsp;

&nbsp;

